,"H376":"man","H3627":"article/utensil","H3027":"hand","H4191":"to die","H1961":"to be","H854":"with","H3318":"come","H6680":"to command","H3808":"not","H6362":"to separate","H4256":"division","H5414":"give","H2595":"spear","H4043":"shield","H7982":"shield","H5975":"stand","H7973":"missile","H3802":"shoulder","H3233":"right","H5704":"till","H8042":"left","H4196":"altar","H5145":"Nazirite vow","H5715":"testimony","H4886":"to anoint","H2421":"to live","H8085":"hear","H6271":"Athaliah","H6963":"voice","H7323":"run","H1984":"to shine","H7200":"see","H5982":"pillar","H3996":"entrance","H2689":"trumpet","H776":"country/planet","H8056":"glad","H8628":"to blow","H7891":"to sing","H7892":"song","H3045":"to know","H7167":"to tear","H899":"treachery","H7195":"conspiracy","H6485":"list","H2428":"Helech","H7713":"rank","H310":"after","H2719":"sword","H7760":"make","H5483":"swallow","H8033":"there","H996":"between","H1168":"Baal","H5422":"to tear","H6754":"image","H7665":"to break","H4977":"Mattan","H2026":"to kill","H6440":"before","H6486":"punishment","H2505":"to divide","H5927":"rise","H5930":"burnt offering","H3789":"to write","H8451":"instruction","H4872":"Moses","H8057":"joy","H2931":"unclean","H117":"great","H4910":"to rule","H3381":"to go down","H8432":"midst","H5945":"high","H3427":"to dwell","H3678":"throne","H4467":"kingdom","H8055":"to rejoice","H8252":"to quiet"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["challoner",5,null,"challoner","To the sabbath.... That is, to perform in your weeks the functions of your office, or the weekly watches."],["haydock",1,null,"haydock","Seventh. Vatican Septuagint, by mistake, has “the eighth.” — Encouraged, or “strengthened.” (Septuagint, &c.) (Haydock) — Captains, whether Levites, or ancient officers of the crown, who were dissatisfied with the usurper, 4 Kings xi."],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","Israel, of which Juda formed a part. (Menochius) — At the time when the author lived, Israel was destroyed, so that there was no danger of a mistake. — Jerusalem, on a sabbath-day, and most likely on one of the three great festivals: (Calmet) Salien (the year of the world 3157) thinks at the Passover, to avoid suspicion. (Menochius)"],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","Do. Though God’s promise was absolute, human means were to be used. (Worthington)"],["haydock",5,null,"haydock","To the sabbath. That is, to perform in your weeks the functions of your office, or the weekly watches. (Challoner) — Porters. Septuagint, “even to the entrance gates.” — House, where Athalia resided, or in the apartments of Joas in the temple. — Foundation. Septuagint, “middle.” Syriac, “of the cooks, or guards.” (Haydock) — It led from the palace up the steps, ver. 21. (Menochius) — Perhaps it was also called Sur, 4 Kings. — But let. This seems to be transposed out of its place from ver. 6."],["haydock",7,null,"haydock","Slain. Athalia ventured to enter; but she was alone, and not much feared. (Calmet)"],["haydock",8,null,"haydock","High. Hebrew, “the priest dismissed not the courses.” (Haydock) — In case of right and necessity, we see here what the high priest could do, though otherwise he would not interfere. (Worthington)"],["haydock",10,null,"haydock","Altar of holocausts, in the court of the priests, while the people stood in their own court. (Tirinus)"],["haydock",11,null,"haydock","Crown. Literally, “diadem.” — Testimony. This is explained in the following sentence, (Haydock) which is not in Hebrew nor in many Latin manuscripts. The Jews understand the phylacteries, Deuteronomy xvii. 18."],["haydock",13,null,"haydock","Step. Hebrew hamudo, “his pillar,” to which he ascended by steps. (Du Hamel) — Entrance into the court of the priests; but the tribune stood in that of the people, where Joas was in his royal attire."],["haydock",16,null,"haydock","Himself, as God’s vicegerent. (Calmet) — A double covenant was made between God and the people, and between the king and his subjects. (Du Hamel)"],["haydock",17,null,"haydock","Idols. Protestants, “images.” (Haydock) — Those are wilfully blind who will not distinguish these from the images of Christ and his saints. (Worthington)"],["haydock",18,null,"haydock","David, which had been long neglected, 1 Paralipomenon xxiv. (Menochius)"],["haydock",20,null,"haydock","Upper gate of the guards, at the back or western end of the temple, chap. v. 5."]],"au":{"challoner":["Richard Challoner",0,0,1781,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/03566a.htm"],"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}